# Crypto Watcher — Smart Contracts

> Phase tags (`MVP`, `Phase 1`, `Phase 2`, `Phase 3`, `Final`) cite
> [ROADMAP](./ROADMAP.mdc). Keep this file in sync with the roadmap and with the
> actual `contracts/` implementation (see the docs-sync rule in `.cursor/rules/`).

> **Product model:** Official project risk scores are published by a vetted governor
> council only. CWT governs **protocol** decisions (reviewer roster, methodology,
> accountability) — not vote-to-rate on individual projects. Legacy `ProjectVoting` /
> reputation-weighted public score contracts remain in the repo from an earlier design
> and are being refactored toward governor-only review authority.

## Tech Stack

- Solidity + Foundry (`forge`, `cast`, `anvil`) — see [README](../README.md).
- OpenZeppelin contracts for `ERC20Votes`, `Governor`, `TimelockController`,
  `AccessControl`.
- Consumed on the frontend via Viem + Wagmi.

## Modular Folder Structure

The contracts package is organized by domain module. Each module owns its
contracts, interfaces, tests and deploy scripts.

```
contracts/
├── foundry.toml
├── project.json                  # Nx targets for forge build/test/fmt  [MVP]
├── remappings.txt
├── lib/                          # forge dependencies (OpenZeppelin, forge-std)
├── src/
│   ├── governance/               # Protocol governance module
│   │   ├── GovernanceToken.sol   # ERC20Votes governance token  [MVP]
│   │   ├── CryptoWatcherGovernor.sol  # Governor (proposals/voting)  [MVP→Final]
│   │   ├── Timelock.sol          # TimelockController             [MVP]
│   │   ├── ProtocolSettings.sol  # Governed protocol params       [MVP]
│   │   └── interfaces/
│   ├── voting/                   # Per-project registry module (legacy name)
│   │   ├── ProjectVoting.sol     # On-chain review record / anchor [MVP] (legacy vote-to-rate being removed)
│   │   ├── ProjectWatcherFactory.sol # Backend-gated submit + registry [MVP]
│   │   └── interfaces/
│   ├── reputation/               # Reviewer credentials module
│   │   ├── ReputationRegistry.sol # Governor eligibility + reviewer weight [MVP→Phase 1]
│   │   └── interfaces/
│   ├── rewards/                  # Reviewer compensation module
│   │   ├── RewardDistributor.sol # Governor compensation + misconduct penalties [Phase 1]
│   │   └── interfaces/
│   ├── access/                   # Shared access control / roles
│   │   └── Roles.sol
│   └── libraries/                # Shared libraries (math, scoring)
├── script/                       # forge deploy scripts (per module)
├── test/                         # mirrors src/ module layout
│   ├── governance/
│   ├── voting/
│   ├── reputation/
│   └── integration/              # Sepolia fork integration tests        [MVP]
└── deployments/                  # per-chain deployed addresses (json)
```

## Modules by Phase

### Governance module — launch requirement
- `GovernanceToken` (`ERC20Votes`): token + delegation support for **protocol**
  governance only. `[MVP]`
- Seed distribution to early protocol participants / treasury. `[MVP]`
- `Timelock` (`TimelockController`) owned by team multisig at launch. `[MVP]`
- `CryptoWatcherGovernor`: proposals for protocol params (reviewer roster changes,
  methodology version, review fees, backend submitter rotation). `[MVP]`
- `ProtocolSettings`: Timelock-owned review methodology and council policy params. `[MVP]`
- Community token-weighted **protocol** proposals, quorum + voting delay. `[Phase 1]`
- Vote delegation UX support for protocol votes. `[Phase 2]`
- Full DAO: treasury + upgrade control governed on-chain. `[Final]`

### Review registry module (folder: `voting/`)
- `ProjectWatcherFactory`: backend-controlled `submitProject(projectId, submitter)`
  callable only by the platform `backend` (users pay for their review off-chain;
  the backend then emits the on-chain record on their behalf). Deploys one registry
  contract per project, records the paying user as submitter, prevents duplicate ids
  and exposes a registry (`votingOf`, `submitterOf`, enumeration).
  `Ownable2Step` + `Pausable`; governance owns it, can rotate the `backend`
  address (`setBackend`) and pause submissions. `[MVP]`
- `ProjectVoting` (legacy): currently implements public vote-to-rate; target state is
  governor-only score publication with on-chain audit trail. Refactor in progress. `[MVP]`
- Indexer-friendly events for published scores, reviewer attestations, methodology
  version and timestamps. `[MVP]`
- Governor-gated score publication (only `GOVERNOR_ROLE` / council members). `[MVP]`
- Multi-chain deployment of project registry contracts. `[Phase 2]`

### Reputation module (reviewer credentials)
- `ReputationRegistry`: governor/reviewer allow-list + accountability weight for
  **council members only** — not public score voting eligibility. `[MVP→Phase 1]`
- Multi-factor reviewer reputation (report quality, timeliness, appeal overturn rate,
  conflict disclosures). `[Phase 1]`
- On-chain reviewer credential references. `[Phase 2]`
- Decentralized expertise verification. `[Final]`

### Rewards module (reviewer compensation)
- `RewardDistributor`: compensate governors for completed reviews; penalties for
  misconduct — **not** rewards for public project score voting. `[Phase 1]`
- Slashing / penalties for governor misconduct (conflicts, falsified reports). `[Phase 1]`
- Sustainable reviewer compensation + treasury funding. `[Final]`

## Scoring

- Official project score published by governor council; methodology version referenced
  on-chain. `[MVP]`
- Score factors enriched with external risk signals to **assist** governors (human-in-the-loop). `[Phase 3]`
- Appeals and re-review workflow (governor council, not token vote). `[Phase 1]`

## Security & Testing

- Foundry unit + fuzz tests per module, CI security scanning. `[MVP]`
- Fork-based integration tests in `test/integration/` exercise the full deploy +
  governance + review-registry lifecycle against a Sepolia fork (`SEPOLIA_RPC_URL`); they
  skip automatically when no RPC is configured. `[MVP]`
- External audits scaling with phase. `[Phase 2 → Final]`
- Formal verification of core contracts. `[Final]`

## Conventions

- One module = one folder under `src/`, with matching `test/` and `script/` folders.
- Interfaces live in each module's `interfaces/` folder.
- Deployed addresses tracked per chain in `deployments/`.
- Use `AccessControl` roles (from `access/Roles.sol`) instead of bare `onlyOwner`.
- Format Solidity with `forge fmt`; repo-level `pnpm run format` runs Prettier for
  TypeScript/React docs and `forge fmt` for contracts. `[MVP]`
